00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:07.910
That number is two one nine, two, David P.
here's the voicemail that's sort of funny,

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.870
but it relates to something we've been thinking
about.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:10.870
Take a listen.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.910
Hey David, Joe from California.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:16.430
Hey, um, have you thought about doing it?

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:22.651
Tour meaning, uh, say you take a month and
you travel to different, um, central areas,

00:00:22.651 --> 00:00:29.980
uh, where you have listeners, we, you meet
up, you do a live broadcast show from there

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.680
at the same time to maybe a voter registration
drive.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:38.140
I'll have a live guest there, greet and at
the same time social, some Birch.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.510
So that would be cool.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.879
Have you thought of that?

00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:43.879
Hi David.

00:00:43.879 --> 00:00:44.879
Yeah.

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:45.879
Yeah,

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:46.879
so I love the idea.

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:49.659
I would love to get to different parts of
the country, including parts of the country.

00:00:49.659 --> 00:00:53.670
I don't typically get to meet viewers, do
live shows, all that stuff.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.559
The concerns are more practical.

00:00:55.559 --> 00:00:57.989
Number one, the amount of logistics for a
tour.

00:00:57.989 --> 00:01:01.550
And now I know people who have done tours,
the logistics are crazy.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:05.670
So if we were to handle it internally, it
would be almost crippling because of the amount

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:09.280
of stuff that would not get done because we're
dealing with the tour logistics.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.720
So we are, I'm talking to my agent, my agent
came to me a couple of weeks ago actually

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:20.880
and said, Hey, I want to go and talk to an
actual tour management company where they

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.250
would set up everything so you don't have
to deal with it.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.250
You would just have to show up.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.160
That would make it much more feasible.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.970
And my manager is actually talking about doing
it.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:32.780
But some other, uh, progressive hosts that,
whose names certainly you would recognize

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.220
that would be very interesting.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:39.240
The other thing is, you know, taking a month
off from the show is basically a nonstarter.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:45.280
Doing the show on the road in addition to
events is, um, that's another set of logistics

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.470
and the show is best when I'm in the studio.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:48.470
That's the reality.

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:53.500
I'm not even sure if I'm going to the conventions
this summer because the best show would be

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:59.570
me being here, having reporters there doing
live coverage via video.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:04.060
Whenever we're at events, I do feel like the
content actually suffers to some degree, so

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.060
that's another question.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:09.550
If we were to do it like a month long tour,
the other possibility is to only do events

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:14.730
around weekends, like Thursday, Friday, Saturday
events, and travel back and forth every week.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:18.359
That is a big undertaking as well, so we're
looking into the tour thing.

00:02:18.359 --> 00:02:20.159
I would love to do it at a personal level.

00:02:20.159 --> 00:02:21.220
I think it would be great.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:25.579
It's the, the devil is in the details as the
kids these days, like to say that does it

